so in related news  to the the the death of expertise the  disregard for science and data and  research  is that the fact that the international  governmental panel on climate change  released its long-awaited report just  the other day  and before i get to some of the key  findings that i find interesting and  alarming i want to talk about an aspect  of american culture that exists within  evangelical christianity  there's this pastor named perry stone  and we're going to get to a clip of him  but  coming from this faith tradition i was  raised an evangelical christian a  conservative christian nationalist if  you will  and  when i was when i was coming up in the  church it was  it was  taught that god gave man dominion over  the earth and because of that we needed  to be good stewards  of god's creation the planet  and it doesn't seem to be that way  anymore  perry stone here who isn't some no-name  you may not know who he is but he's got  a youtube channel of like 650 000 people  he's the leader of a congregation people  listen to him they look up to him they  admire him  they honor him with leadership  and he is saying in this clip i'm  getting ready to play  screw it let it burn  yeah climate change real but we don't  care because jesus is coming back in  revelation chapter 20 when christ comes  back to earth and sets up his kingdom  he's going to change  everything and there's going to be a  thousand years of peace and so the sons  of god and these are the children of god  these are believers who return with  christ who set up the kingdom for a  thousand years we're going to see a  complete change in the earth and that  what we call the travail of creation or  the travel of the earth will cease when  the messiah returns so those who  criticize believers now for not being  you know environmentally concerned or  whatever we know how the book ends we  know where this is going we know how in  the end when messiah comes back look  folk can i say something to you and say  it in love it's wonderful to do all that  we can to help the planet but at the  same time if you know what the prophecy  says you know what's coming and you know  that real peace real joy and and  everything that men want will only  happen with the return of the messiah  and you can see that all through the  book of zechariah you can see it in the  writings of isaiah and that messiah  without a doubt is one man and it's  jesus christ that is alarming  that is an admission that yeah listen a  lot of christians we just don't care  about it because we're waiting for jesus  our faith  is  paramount to anything else  we're gambling on the fact that jesus is  going to be coming back to save us  so let it burn  that is that is a remarkable admission  that i believe is held by millions of  people  and it is  very difficult  to pry that viewpoint away from people  when when it is not substantiated by  fact  when it is only an emotional response  to  what is happening in our world  and let's talk a little bit about what's  happening in our world specifically some  of the key findings of the ipcc report  one  is that  humans are to blame  for for climate change without a doubt  we are in a situation now where it  cannot be denied  reading from this article from reuters  the intergovernmental panel on climate  change the ipcc used its strongest terms  yet to assert that humans are causing  climate change  with the first line of its report  summary reading quote  it is unequivocal that human influence  has warmed the atmosphere ocean  and land  it is unequivocal  the stark language marked a shift from  previous ipcc reports which had said it  was extremely likely that industrial  activity was to blame  there is no uncertainty language in this  sentence because there is no uncertainty  that global warming is caused by human  activity and the burning of fossil  that was the  the ipcc co-author  um frederic otto he's a climatologist at  the university of oxford  these are learned individuals  they are well versed in climatology  they're not  making wild claims like a mike lindell  with zero expertise  these people have dedicated their lives  to one single topic  to get it right  to be an expert  not to be fueled by dunning-kruger mania  another key takeaway  is that the temperatures are going to  continue to rise  even the severest of cuts are unlikely  to prevent global warming of 1.5 degrees  celsius over pre-industrial temperatures  without immediate steep emissions cuts  though average temperatures could cruise  past two degrees celsius by the end  of the century  that is scary  and it may seem like a long ways away  the end of the century  but  if you're getting ready to have a kid  they could very well be alive then  we're talking about  protecting the climate and the planet  for posterity's sake  this is a literal  existential crisis that we're facing  what's the saying about uh it's an  honorable man who plants a tree the  shade of which he'll never enjoy  i'm sure i botched it but it's something  like that  and are we gonna be the perry stones of  the world or are we gonna plant trees  the shade of which we'll never enjoy  another  key finding here is one that we all are  witnessing in real time  and that that is that extreme weather  events are getting more and more common  and more  and more extreme  they can tie this to what's called  attribution science it's no longer  guessing whether or not uh climate  change is is the responsibility is the  the triggering factor for the wildfires  here in california or in australia or  anywhere else around the world  it's no longer up in the air whether  flooding events  are caused  by  the climate change they know now  attribution science  that's something you should familiarize  yourself with  in the past people would say you can't  say anything about any individual event  said ipcc co-author michael weiner a  climate scientist at the lawrence  berkeley national laboratory in  california  but now we can actually make  quantitative statements about extreme  weather events  this is serious  now listen the report does say  that where we if we were to to stop it  that some of these changes are going to  happen whether we we could go to zero  carbon emission right now and some of  these changes are still going to take  place  but they're saying it's not too late  this is an extreme problem  i believe it's going to take extreme  measures  to get it under control  whether that be the new green new deal  whether that be some of the the  initiatives that biden has proposed  but it's going to take more than just  letting it burn because of jesus  that is a fact

